  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.1.16 build: enable EnforceCodeStyleInBuild centrally (#1941)\n        v0.1.15 fix(sonar): pass CancellationToken and fix new-code issues (#1938)\n        v0.2.6 fix: report a diagnostic for nested strong types (#250)\n        v0.2.5 fix: report a diagnostic for generic options types (#249)\n        v0.2.4 chore: promote IDE0290 to warning\n        v0.2.3 chore: promote IDE0011 to warning\n        v0.2.2 test: complete StrongType rename and fill SourceGenerators test gaps\n        v0.2.1 fix: remove Workspaces reference from source generators (RS1038)\n        v0.2.0 feat: classify AutoRegisterService by architectural layer\n        v0.1.14 chore: solution cleanup - namespaces, XML doc formatting, test folder alignment\n\t\t\tv0.1.13 - Bundle AStarDev.SourceAnalyzers.dll (ASTAROPT002) into this package so consumers of AStarDev.SourceGenerators receive its diagnostics without a separate package reference.\n\t\t\tv0.1.12 - Fix StrongIdGenerator emitting 'System.Type Id' instead of 'System.Guid Id' when [StrongType] is applied with no explicit type argument.\n\t\t\tv0.1.11 - Actual fix: drop custom nuspec (NuspecFile mode skipped _GetPackageFiles, package had zero DLLs); move Attributes DLL out of lib/ so no TFM-scoped asset restricts compatibility.\n\t\t\tv0.1.10 - Fix NuGet package framework compatibility: empty dependency group for all-frameworks support (did not work, nuspec mode broken).\n\t\t\tv0.1.9 - Framework compatibility fix attempt (published with restrictions).\n\t\t\tv0.1.8 - Fix NuGet package structure: analyzer DLL and Attributes DLL were missing due to MSBuild target ordering.\n\t\t\tv0.1.7 - Fix bug in AutoRegisterServiceAttribute detection/code generation.\n\t\t\tv0.1.6 - Fix build and packaging issues.\n\t\t\tv0.1.5 - Update dependencies to latest Roslyn versions.\n\t\t\tv0.1.4 - Add missing namespace in generated ServiceRegistrations class.\n\t\t\t- Rename ServiceAttribute to AutoRegisterServiceAttribute for clarity",
